   are Tailwind's own palette, tuned as pastel-on-dark. They compile to
   `color: var(--color-red-400)`, so re-declaring the variable in the light scope fixes
   every use, hover/variant included, with no per-class rules. Shades 100-400 map to a
   deeper shade; 500+ (solid fills, buttons) are untouched. Dark islands restore the
   stock values. */
const HUES = ["red", "rose", "amber", "emerald", "green", "sky", "cyan", "violet", "purple", "blue", "yellow", "orange", "teal", "indigo", "pink", "fuchsia", "lime"];
